<div class="sl">Likutay Halachos &middot; Yoreh De&rsquo;ah, Part Two</div>
<div class="mt">Laws of the Redemption of the Firstborn</div>
<div class="st">Hilchos Pidyon HaBechor &mdash; Halacha Two</div>
<div class="dv">&middot; &middot; &#10022; &middot; &middot;</div>

<div class="snb">Based upon the discourse beginning <em>Meishra d&rsquo;sakkina b&rsquo;mai katli lei</em> etc. (Siman 30) &mdash; see there well.</div>

<!-- INTRO -->
<div class="sh">Introduction &mdash; The Dales, the Four Kingdoms, and Chesed</div>

<p class="ni">It is stated there: that sometimes the aspect of the <em>Dales</em> [the letter <em>dalet</em>] falls &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em> [lower wisdom], the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> [kingship]. And then the forces of evil have sustenance from there, and from this are formed the four kingdoms, which is the wicked kingdom, the kingdom of Amalek that comprises them all &mdash; the aspect of <em>reishis goyim Amalek</em> [the first of the nations is Amalek]. And one must endeavour to cut and separate the aspect of the <em>dalet</em> from them, so that they have no sustenance from there. And this is accomplished through <em>chesed</em> [loving-kindness], the aspect of Avraham. For through this one cuts the aspects of the four &mdash; the aspects of <em>Malchus</em> &mdash; from them, in the aspect of <em>kitzru l&rsquo;fi chesed</em> [reap according to kindness] etc. See there.</p>

<!-- SECTION 2 -->
<div class="sh">Section 2 &mdash; The Firstborn as Malchus; Giving the Bechor to the Kohen</div>

<p class="ni">And this is the aspect of the commandment of the firstborn (<em>bechor</em>) that belongs to the Kohen. For the firstborn is the aspect of <em>Malchus</em>, the aspect of <em>af ani bechor etnenhu</em> [I too shall make him a firstborn], said of King Mashiach. For the firstborn is the first birth, and all births are the aspect of the revelation of His kingship blessed-be-He. For the essential revelation of His kingship blessed-be-He is through the creation of the world, as is known. And therefore the more creatures are born and come into the world, the more His kingship blessed-be-He is revealed. And therefore the firstborn, who is the first birth, is the aspect of the initial revelation of <em>Malchus</em> as mentioned.</p>

<p>For birth is the aspect of the contraction (<em>tzimtzum</em>) of <em>da&rsquo;as</em> [knowledge] from <em>chochmah ila&rsquo;ah</em> [supernal wisdom] to <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em> [lower wisdom] &mdash; through which the birth comes about. It follows that birth is the aspect of <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em>, the aspect of <em>Malchus</em>. And the essential [birth] is the first birth, which is the <em>bechor</em>, which is the aspect of the beginning of the revelation. For everything follows the beginning. And therefore the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> is called by the name <em>bechor</em>, in the aspect of <em>af ani bechor etnenhu</em> said of King Mashiach as mentioned.</p>

<p>And therefore when the firstborn is born &mdash; which is the aspect of the revelation of <em>Malchus</em> &mdash; and at the moment when the revelation of holy <em>Malchus</em> begins, then <em>zeh l&rsquo;umas zeh</em> [this opposite this], for then the wicked kingdom wishes to prevail and draw sustenance, heaven forbid, from the holy <em>Malchus</em> that is its counterpart. And the wicked kingdom is also the aspect of <em>bechor</em> &mdash; the aspect of the kingdom of Esav-Amalek which is <em>bechor</em>. And for this reason Yaakov strove greatly to purchase the birthright from Esav, in order to subjugate the wicked kingdom under the holy <em>Malchus</em>, for the essential <em>Malchus</em> is the aspect of <em>bechor</em> as mentioned. And when he purchased his birthright from him, through this the kingdom of the wicked Esav was nullified, which is the wicked kingdom.</p>

<p>And therefore when a firstborn is born among Yisrael, one must give him to the Kohen. For when the firstborn is born &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> as mentioned &mdash; one must then endeavour to separate and cut him from the wicked kingdom, the <em>bechor</em> of the <em>Sitra Achra</em> as mentioned. And this is accomplished through the Kohen, the man of <em>chesed</em>. For through <em>chesed</em>, through this one cuts the holy <em>Malchus</em> from the wicked kingdom, as explained well in the aforementioned discourse. And therefore through giving the firstborn to the Kohen, through this one cuts and separates the holy <em>Malchus</em> &mdash; the aspect of the holy <em>bechor</em> &mdash; from the wicked kingdom, through the Kohen the man of <em>chesed</em>, in the aspect of <em>kitzru l&rsquo;fi chesed</em> as mentioned. For the Kohen is the aspect of <em>chesed</em>, the aspect of Avraham, of whom it is said <em>atah kohen l&rsquo;olam</em> [you are a priest forever].</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of what is brought: that before the firstborn is redeemed, the <em>Sitra Achra</em> has dominion [over him]. And through the redemption one removes him from their domain &mdash; that is, as mentioned. For they are attached to draw sustenance from the aspect of the <em>bechor</em> precisely, which was the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> from which comes their sustenance as mentioned. And through the Kohen the man of <em>chesed</em> one cuts and separates him from them, as mentioned.</p>

<!-- SECTION 3 -->
<div class="sh">Section 3 &mdash; The Five Shekalim: Rectifying Wealth and Cutting Off the Sitra Achra</div>

<p class="ni">And this is the aspect of the redemption (<em>pidyon</em>) with five <em>shekalim</em> that are given to the Kohen. For it is stated there in the aforementioned discourse that the essential means of meriting the aspect of <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em> &mdash; the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> mentioned above &mdash; is through hating monetary gain (<em>sonei betza</em>), for one must hate money with ultimate hatred etc., see there. For the essential sustenance of the wicked kingdom comes through the desire for money, for from there is their essential nourishment &mdash; from wealth that is not in holiness &mdash; as is also explained elsewhere.</p>

<p>And therefore when one wishes to redeem the firstborn from the Kohen, one must then rectify one&rsquo;s money and wealth &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> &mdash; so that the <em>Sitra Achra</em> should have no sustenance from the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> through the money. For their essential sustenance is from there. And therefore one must give money to the Kohen. And through this one breaks the desire for money by taking one&rsquo;s money and giving it to the Kohen. And through this very act one also rectifies the money and wealth &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>Malchus</em> &mdash; by giving the money to the Kohen. For the Kohen rectifies money and wealth, since he is the man of <em>chesed</em> who cuts the holy <em>Malchus</em> from the <em>Sitra Achra</em> through <em>chesed</em>.</p>

<p>And therefore this money and wealth that comes into his hand from the Yisrael &mdash; that is, the five <em>shekalim</em> that the Kohen takes &mdash; immediately when the money comes into his hand it is cut and separated from the <em>Sitra Achra</em>, from the wicked kingdom, through <em>chesed</em> as mentioned. And when the money and wealth &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>Malchus</em>, from which the essential sustenance of the wicked kingdom comes through wealth that is not in holiness as mentioned &mdash; is rectified: then immediately when the wealth is rectified the firstborn returns to Yisrael. For now it is already permitted for the firstborn to be in the possession of the Yisrael, since they have no sustenance from the aspect of the firstborn&rsquo;s <em>Malchus</em> through the five <em>shekalim</em> he gave to the Kohen, through which the money and wealth were rectified and cut and separated from the <em>Sitra Achra</em>, from the wicked kingdom. And now they no longer have sustenance from the holy <em>Malchus</em>, the aspect of <em>bechor</em>, for their essential sustenance is through the wealth as mentioned.</p>

<!-- SECTION 4 -->
<div class="sh">Section 4 &mdash; Five Shekalim = the Letter Heh; Twenty Silver = Two Yuds United</div>

<p class="ni">And therefore one must give five <em>shekalim</em> precisely. For <em>Malchus</em> is the aspect of <em>heh</em> [the letter <em>heh</em>, numerically five] as is known. And when <em>Malchus</em> is in exile, heaven forbid, and they draw sustenance from it, it is in the aspect of <em>dales</em> &mdash; the aspect of poverty and indigence &mdash; for the wealth is blemished, heaven forbid, and they draw sustenance from there, heaven forbid, and the wealth flows to them, heaven forbid. And then the holy <em>Malchus</em> is in the aspect of poverty and indigence, the aspect of <em>dales</em>.</p>

<p>But when the wealth and <em>Malchus</em> are elevated to holiness, then it is the aspect of <em>heh</em>, for all the wealth and all the influences return to holiness. And when <em>Malchus</em> is in the aspect of wealth, then it is the aspect of <em>heh</em>. And this is the aspect of the five <em>shekalim</em> given to the Kohen, for through this the wealth returns to holiness through the Kohen the man of <em>chesed</em>, who cuts the <em>dales</em> from the wicked kingdom. And then <em>Malchus</em> is in the aspect of <em>heh</em>, in the aspect of wealth, in the aspect of <em>va-harikosi lachem berachah ad b&rsquo;li dai</em> [and I will pour out for you a blessing without limit].</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of twenty silver (<em>esrim kesef</em>). For the five <em>shekalim</em> given to the Kohen are twenty silver &mdash; this being the aspect of the rectification of the holy <em>Malchus</em>, the aspect of <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em> that ascends from the wicked kingdom through the Kohen the man of <em>chesed</em>. And then <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em> is joined with <em>chochmah ila&rsquo;ah</em>, from which is the essential sustenance of <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em>, as is explained and understood in the aforementioned discourse. And when <em>chochmah tata&rsquo;ah</em> and <em>chochmah ila&rsquo;ah</em> are joined together, this is the aspect of twenty silver. For they are two <em>yuds</em> [each <em>yud</em> = ten] &mdash; the aspect of <em>asarah asarah ha-kaf</em> [ten ten the <em>kaf</em>], as is known.</p>

<!-- SECTION 5 -->
<div class="sh">Section 5 &mdash; Rashi on the Five Shekalim; Yosef&rsquo;s Sale; the Exodus and Plunder of Egypt</div>

<p class="ni">And this is what Rashi explains regarding the reason for the five <em>shekalim</em> of the redemption of the firstborn: thus was the sale of Yosef, for twenty silver, since he was the firstborn of Rachel etc. For the commandment of the firstborn was given to Bnei Yisrael immediately upon their going out from Egypt. For the essential Exodus from Egypt depended on this: to subjugate the <em>bechor</em> of the <em>Sitra Achra</em> and to bring out from there the holy <em>bechor</em>. For the essential exile of Egypt began through the sale of Yosef, who was the firstborn. And through this they brought, as it were, the holy <em>bechor</em> &mdash; who is the aspect of the holy <em>Malchus</em> &mdash; into the exile of Egypt. And particularly because they sold him for twenty silver and blemished the wealth, as mentioned.</p>

<p>And therefore through this precisely the matter unfolded and they descended to Egypt, for they gave power to the kingdom of Egypt, the wicked kingdom, through selling to them the holy <em>bechor</em> who is Yosef as mentioned. And therefore it was impossible for them to leave until Hashem struck all the firstborn of Egypt, in order to subjugate the <em>bechor</em> of the <em>Sitra Achra</em> that was drawing sustenance from the holy <em>bechor</em> &mdash; from which came their essential power as mentioned.</p>

<p>And therefore when they left, Moshe himself took the bones of Yosef with him. For in this depended the essential redemption: through returning and bringing out the holy <em>bechor</em> &mdash; the aspect of Yosef &mdash; from the wicked kingdom. And what Yisrael took of the wealth of Egypt and all their riches is all one aspect, for they are all one, and the entire essential redemption depended on this. For the essential redemption comes through subjugating the wicked kingdom, the <em>bechor</em> of the <em>Sitra Achra</em>, and elevating from there the holy <em>Malchus</em> which is the aspect of the holy <em>bechor</em>, the aspect of Yosef. And then one must bring out all the wealth from the <em>Sitra Achra</em> and bring it into holiness, as mentioned.</p>

<p>And as our Sages of blessed memory said: all of Yisrael were occupied with the plunder, and Moshe was occupied with the bones of Yosef. For in truth it is all one. For what Moshe took &mdash; the bones of Yosef, the holy <em>bechor</em> returned and brought out from the wicked kingdom &mdash; and what Yisrael took &mdash; the wealth of Egypt and all their riches &mdash; is all one aspect. And the entire essential redemption depended on this. For the essential redemption comes through subjugating the wicked kingdom, the <em>bechor</em> of the <em>Sitra Achra</em>, and elevating from there the holy <em>Malchus</em> which is the aspect of the holy <em>bechor</em>, the aspect of Yosef. And then all the wealth must be brought out from the <em>Sitra Achra</em> into holiness, as mentioned.</p>

<p>And therefore it was then a great commandment to take the plunder of Egypt, and Hashem blessed-be-He warned them greatly about this, as explained in the verse there. For it is the aspect of rectifying the holy <em>Malchus</em>, on which the essential redemption depends, as mentioned. And therefore when they left Egypt they were immediately commanded the commandment of the firstborn &mdash; to redeem him with twenty silver, just as was the sale of Yosef through which they descended into the wicked exile of Egypt. Correspondingly, in reverse: at every time when a firstborn is born, and one must ensure that the wicked kingdom should have no sustenance from there, heaven forbid, one must give twenty silver to the Kohen, the man of <em>chesed</em>. And through this one cuts the holy <em>Malchus</em> from them in the aspect of <em>kitzru l&rsquo;fi chesed</em> as mentioned.</p>

<!-- SECTION 6 -->
<div class="sh">Section 6 &mdash; Opening the Womb; <em>Bechor Peter Kol Rechem</em></div>

<p class="ni">This too is the aspect of what Rabbeinu explains there in the aforementioned matter in another place: that through this the womb of a woman in difficult labour (<em>makshah leileid</em>) is opened, in the aspect of <em>daltei vitni</em> [the doors of my belly]. And this is the aspect of <em>chatcho l&rsquo;arba</em> [cutting it into four] &mdash; see there and understand well. And this is the aspect of <em>bechor peter kol rechem</em> [the firstborn that opens every womb] that one gives to the Kohen the man of <em>chesed</em>. For through <em>chesed</em> is accomplished the aspect of <em>chatcho l&rsquo;arba</em>, through which the birth takes place. And the essential birth is the first birth, for the essential is the beginning. Understand this well.</p>

<div class="closing">Baruch Hashem l&rsquo;olam, Amen v&rsquo;Amen.</div>

